Issue #416:
Charter: #305
Depends-on: #415

## Context

Part of charter #305 (Queue visibility & state machine overhaul). This leaf restructures the QueuePanel layout so it is always visible regardless of scroll position or number of agents.

**Prerequisite:** issue #415 (leaf-327) must be merged first — the final QueuePanel prop interface is established there and must be stable before the render tree is restructured here.

## Background / problem

When there are many agents in the loop (synthetic + real), the queue panel is embedded inside the scrollable agent/charter board and gets lost. Operators cannot see the queue. The fix: move QueuePanel into a dedicated, always-visible block (sticky sidebar or fixed top panel).

## Changes required

### 1. `ui/app/src/App.tsx` — layout restructure

Find the render section where `<QueuePanel .../>` currently lives inside the scrollable board container. Extract it to a sibling element that is outside (and rendered independently of) the scrollable area. The queue panel must be visible at all times, not just when the user scrolls to it.

### 2. `ui/app/src/styles.css` — sticky/fixed positioning

Add a CSS class (e.g. `.queue-panel--sticky`) that positions the panel as a sticky sidebar or fixed top block. Requirements:
- Panel is always visible (does not scroll away with agent cards)
- Does not overlap or conflict with agent-card / charter-card layout
- Works correctly at various viewport widths (responsive at minimum to the widths already supported by the app)

### Prop interface to use (from leaf-327 / issue #415)

```typescript
interface QueuePanelProps {
  queueOrder: number[]
  savedOrder: number[]
  board: Milestone[]
  isLoopRunning: boolean
  onQueueChange: (order: number[]) => Promise<void>
  onLaunch: () => Promise<void>
}
```

Do not change these props — leaf-329 also depends on them.

## Scope boundary

UI-only: `ui/app/src/App.tsx` and `ui/app/src/styles.css`. Gateway and launcher untouched.

## Acceptance (machine)

- check: cd ui/app && npm run build
- check: cd ui/app && npx tsc --noEmit